name o4-07-flares-1
timeout 120

# CAMPAIGN O4, SORTIE 7 OF 10 — THE INFRARED SHOT AGAINST A DEFENDING TARGET, and the campaign's only
# mission whose subject is a MAGAZINE. doc/campaigns/o4-gaf-mig29g-dact.md mission 7.
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION, as the spec states it: both dispensers already work through the same
# deterministic seduction model (sensors/FBIrstSystem::SelectFlare — two received irradiances, I/r^2, no
# die), so the asymmetry is no longer PRESENCE but SIZE: ALE-47 60/60 against BVP-30-26 30/30. Does that
# difference show up over a full engagement?
#
# IT CANNOT BE ANSWERED BY ONE SHOT, so this file is built to run the smaller magazine dry and then
# shoot. TWO BRANCHES, 22 km apart, identical in every number but the airframes:
#   BRANCH A — viper5 (F-16) 4 km astern of fulcrum5 (MiG-29), 40 kt in hand, pickle at t=32.
#              fulcrum5 throws PRGM 3 at t = 6, 11, 16, 21, 26, 31, 36, 41.
#   BRANCH B — fulcrum6 (MiG-29) 4 km astern of viper6 (F-16), the same 40 kt, the same pickle at t=32.
#              viper6 throws the SAME eight dispenses at the SAME eight instants.
# PRGM 3 is FLARE-only and IDENTICAL on both modules (2 cartridges per burst, 4 salvos 1.0 s apart =
# 8 per dispense — modules/f16/FBF16Cmds.cpp, modules/mig29/FBMig29Cmds.cpp), so the two jets throw at
# exactly the same rate and the only thing that differs is how long they can keep it up. [MESS] the MiG
# is DRY at t = 23.8 s (cm_flare 30 -> 0, and the dispenses briefed for t = 26, 31, 36, 41 come back
# `cm_dispense rejected reason=depleted`); the F-16 is dry at t = 42.7 s, all eight dispenses accepted.
# 18.9 seconds of magazine. The round is pickled at t=32 and arrives at t=41.0 — inside that window.
#
# THE DISPENSE LINE IS SPELLED `brief_chaff_s` ON BOTH SIDES, and it throws FLARES: the briefed
# dispense plays the SELECTED programme, and PRGM 3 is flare-only. The spelling is not a choice —
# modules/f16/FBF16Module accepts only `brief_chaff_s` while modules/mig29/FBMig29Module accepts both
# spellings, so the symmetric file has to use the one both modules answer to. mig29-r73.fbm's `flint`
# does the same thing for the same reason.
#
# THE ASTERN GEOMETRY IS THE R-73's OWN DOCUMENTED EMPLOYMENT (doc/modules/mig29/weapons.md §3.3, and
# duel-merge-stern.fbm measures it as a fight), and it is used for BOTH branches so the two rounds are
# compared at the same aspect. NEITHER DEFENDER AUTO-DISPENSES and neither could: the 9-12 has no
# missile-approach warning system (doc/modules/mig29/defence-rwr-cm.md §5) and the F-16 has none in this
# tree either, so an infrared launch is answered only by a BRIEFED throw. That is the honest limit of
# this mission and it is the reason the schedule is briefed rather than triggered.
#
# READING RULE: the verdict is events.log, not the exit code. Read `cmds DISPENSE` counts per unit and
# the `cmds_flare` telemetry column going to zero, then `irst FLARE_SEDUCED` / `FLARE_RESOLVED` on each
# round's own seeker, then the two DETONATION lines' missM. Expect exit 3 (TIMEOUT): one branch's
# shooter meets its `kill`, the other's does not, and a miss is not a mission verdict. Both shooters
# declare `kill unit` as BOOKKEEPING only — without it a defender's destruction is an unexpected loss
# and would end the run before the other branch has flown (doc/missions/verdict.md).

unit viper5
  team friendly
  module f16
  spawn 55.20000 13.53000 5000 90.0 340       # BRANCH A shooter: 4.0 km astern, 40 kt in hand
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set datalink off
  set fcr_mode acm_hud
  set fcr_range_nm 40
  set store 1 aim9
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set brief_release_s 32                      # after the MiG's magazine is out, before the F-16's is
  wp 55.20000 14.60000 5000 340
  objective kill unit fulcrum5

unit fulcrum5
  team hostile
  module mig29
  spawn 55.20000 13.59300 5000 90.0 300       # BRANCH A defender: straight, level, dispensing
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set n019_mode off
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 3                          # FLARE only — an infrared shot; chaff has nothing to work on
  set cmds_chaff 30
  set cmds_flare 30                           # BVP-30-26: HALF the F-16's magazine, and the subject
  set brief_chaff_s 6
  set brief_chaff_s 11
  set brief_chaff_s 16
  set brief_chaff_s 21
  set brief_chaff_s 26
  set brief_chaff_s 31
  set brief_chaff_s 36
  set brief_chaff_s 41
  wp 55.20000 14.60000 5000 300

unit fulcrum6
  team hostile
  module mig29
  spawn 55.40000 13.53000 5000 90.0 340       # BRANCH B shooter, 22 km north: the identical geometry
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set n019_mode cc                            # the narrow auto-locking pattern with the gate opened,
  set n019_range_nm 40                        # as mig29-r73.fbm uses for the same shot
  set n019_emission illum
  set store 1 r73
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set brief_release_s 32
  wp 55.40000 14.60000 5000 340
  objective kill unit viper6

unit viper6
  team friendly
  module f16
  spawn 55.40000 13.59300 5000 90.0 300       # BRANCH B defender: the same schedule, twice the magazine
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set datalink off
  set fcr_mode off
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 3
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60                           # ALE-47: 60/60
  set brief_chaff_s 6
  set brief_chaff_s 11
  set brief_chaff_s 16
  set brief_chaff_s 21
  set brief_chaff_s 26
  set brief_chaff_s 31
  set brief_chaff_s 36
  set brief_chaff_s 41
  wp 55.40000 14.60000 5000 300

unit hulkwest
  module target_soft
  team friendly
  spawn 55.20000 12.60000 ground 90.0 0

unit hulkeast
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 55.20000 14.60000 ground 270.0 0
